# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for scripts/sanitizers.sh.
#
# tokio's I/O driver hands each socket's ScheduledIo to the thread that
# polls epoll through the kernel: its address is epoll's token, registered
# with epoll_ctl on one thread and returned by epoll_wait on another. That
# orders the two, but in the kernel, where ThreadSanitizer cannot see it;
# so every access to a ScheduledIo made before its registration (Arc::new
# writing it, for a start) "races" with the poller's first. Every report
# the tests gave before this line was of that kind (docs/SANITIZERS.md).
race:tokio::runtime::io::scheduled_io
